WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.137 --> 00:00:03.178
- You know, to be great 
I think you have to fight.

00:00:03.178 --> 00:00:04.915
(slow music)

00:00:04.915 --> 00:00:07.259
And I very much 
think that my success

00:00:07.259 --> 00:00:10.370
is a product of 
some level of skill,

00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:13.324
but I do think I win
because I outwork people.

00:00:13.324 --> 00:00:14.356
I really do believe that.

00:00:14.356 --> 00:00:17.408
I do believe that 100%.

00:00:17.408 --> 00:00:20.526
And I'm not sure that if my
dad didn't set that example

00:00:20.526 --> 00:00:22.605
that I'd even have the ability

00:00:22.605 --> 00:00:25.438
to think one could 
work that hard.

00:00:27.303 --> 00:00:30.480
The fact that I've been
working 19 hours a day

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:33.573
everyday for the last
20 years is easy for me.

00:00:33.573 --> 00:00:35.138
It's the only gear I knew, right?

00:00:35.138 --> 00:00:36.484
I was poor.

00:00:36.484 --> 00:00:38.154
I sucked shit at school.

00:00:38.154 --> 00:00:39.868
It was the only gear I have.

00:00:39.868 --> 00:00:41.564
You know, I think you 
need to recognize

00:00:41.564 --> 00:00:44.714
that your biggest advantage

00:00:44.714 --> 00:00:47.363
is that you're hungrier
than your competitor.

00:00:47.363 --> 00:00:51.797
And that if you are not
applying your one advantage,

00:00:51.797 --> 00:00:54.071
which is your 
work ethic and the hours

00:00:54.071 --> 00:00:56.295
that you have to 
put into your business,

00:00:56.295 --> 00:00:57.659
well then you're 
going to come up short.

00:00:57.659 --> 00:01:02.014
I sit here with enormous
assumptions around all of you,

00:01:02.014 --> 00:01:05.346
that you're just too
soft to beat me, right?

00:01:05.346 --> 00:01:07.105
That I think that 
you've had it better.

00:01:07.105 --> 00:01:09.886
And that, that alone doesn't
allow you to beat me.

00:01:09.886 --> 00:01:12.232
Somebody will come with the
counter cultural point of view

00:01:12.232 --> 00:01:14.912
and be like, "Gary, that's
cool, but I don't have

00:01:14.912 --> 00:01:17.839
"to work that hard because
I'm working smarter."

00:01:17.839 --> 00:01:18.771
Yeah, me too, asshole.

00:01:18.771 --> 00:01:21.438
I work hard and smart, now what?

00:01:22.638 --> 00:01:24.701
Look, there's a 
12 hour, 10 hour,

00:01:24.701 --> 00:01:27.181
8 hour, 15 hour work day.

00:01:27.181 --> 00:01:31.297
You can finish a lot of things
in those 18, 12, 9 hours,

00:01:31.297 --> 00:01:33.055
or you can finish 
medium amounts of things

00:01:33.055 --> 00:01:34.452
or lightweight things.

00:01:34.452 --> 00:01:37.049
People focus on too 
many small details.

00:01:37.049 --> 00:01:38.488
Way too many people in this
room are going to spend

00:01:38.488 --> 00:01:39.820
the next 30, 
40 years of their lives

00:01:39.820 --> 00:01:41.806
trying to check the 
boxes of the things

00:01:41.806 --> 00:01:44.234
that they're not as good at,
and that you're going to waste

00:01:44.234 --> 00:01:46.248
a fuckload of time and lose.

00:01:46.248 --> 00:01:48.598
I highly recommend 
for all you hustlers,

00:01:48.598 --> 00:01:50.741
is there's a lot of you,
there's a lot of you,

00:01:50.741 --> 00:01:51.574
that are always talking about,

00:01:51.574 --> 00:01:53.282
"Gary, I do work hard."

00:01:53.282 --> 00:01:54.115
And you do.

00:01:54.115 --> 00:01:55.308
You work for 16 hours.

00:01:55.308 --> 00:01:58.382
Some people just don't
have the attention span

00:01:58.382 --> 00:02:01.303
or the capacity to remember.

00:02:01.303 --> 00:02:03.866
Or like, there's a lot
of things I can't learn.

00:02:03.866 --> 00:02:05.013
I was a very poor student

00:02:05.013 --> 00:02:07.475
because the subject 
matter bored me.

00:02:07.475 --> 00:02:10.995
And if I was forced to
become great at understanding

00:02:10.995 --> 00:02:14.857
the great artists of the 20th
century, I'm in big trouble.

00:02:14.857 --> 00:02:18.496
And so, I would tell people
to bet on their strengths.

00:02:18.496 --> 00:02:20.062
You need to bet 
on your strengths

00:02:20.062 --> 00:02:22.390
and don't give a fuck
about what you suck at.

00:02:22.390 --> 00:02:24.788
And to put themselves 
in a position to win

00:02:24.788 --> 00:02:27.921
with their strengths
because that is absolutely

00:02:27.921 --> 00:02:30.588
the straightest line to success.

00:02:32.748 --> 00:02:34.859
Greatness comes from adversity

00:02:34.859 --> 00:02:37.859
and looking the challenge

00:02:37.859 --> 00:02:40.608
in the eye, and having
the intestinal fortitude

00:02:43.338 --> 00:02:45.588
to step up and go after it.

00:02:45.588 --> 00:02:47.788
(light piano music)

